<!-- This page describes a numerical research candidate, not validated hardware. -->
= Helium DADA domestic-freezer candidate =

This configuration is an exploratory first-level simulation of a compacted
helium DADA refrigerator operating between reservoirs representative of a
domestic freezer in warm ambient conditions. It demonstrates an encouraging
thermodynamic operating point; it is '''not''' a tested appliance, a certified
energy figure or a completed heat-exchanger design.

[[File:publication_helium_freezer_cycle.png|thumb|center|900px|Computed periodic
cycle of helium freezer candidate 001. Positive cold-side heat rate means heat
absorbed by the gas. S and L are the small and large cylinders; C and H are the
cold and hot heat exchangers.]]

[[File:publication_helium_freezer_mechanism.gif|thumb|center|900px|Configured
four-bar motion and cylinder-volume phasing over one revolution. Cylinder bores
are visually enlarged and piston rods shortened for clarity; this clean
illustration is not a manufacturing drawing.]]

== Comparison boundary ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Quantity !! Value
|-
| Nominal frozen compartment || 255.15 K (-18 °C)
|-
| Nominal ambient || 305.15 K (32 °C)
|-
| Cold reservoir || 250.15 K (-23 °C), including a 5 K approach
|-
| Hot reservoir || 310.15 K (37 °C), including a 5 K approach
|-
| Reservoir temperature lift || 60 K
|-
| Carnot COP between reservoirs || 4.169
|}

No cabinet thermal conductance or measured cabinet load is assumed. The
machine's 20.24 W cooling capacity must therefore not be presented as sufficient
for every domestic freezer.

== Thermodynamic configuration ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Value
|-
| Working fluid || Calorically perfect ideal helium
|-
| Gas constants || R = 2077.1 J/(kg K), Cp = 5193.0 J/(kg K), Cv = 3115.9 J/(kg K)
|-
| Initial filling state || 5.000 bar absolute at 298.15 K
|-
| Total helium inventory || 5.956 g
|-
| Rotational speed || 2.000 rpm
|-
| Valve model || Continuous ideal pressure-driven diode, zero threshold
|}

The solver integrates masses and internal energies in S, L, C and H. Pressure
and temperature are reconstructed from that state. Finite heat transfer obeys
<code>Qdot = UA (T_reservoir - T_HX)</code>; isothermal behavior is never
imposed.

== Geometry and imposed kinematics ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Element !! Minimum volume !! Maximum volume / swept volume
|-
| Small cylinder S || 0.0594 L || 5.9994 L / 5.940 L swept
|-
| Large cylinder L || 0.0660 L || 6.6660 L / 6.600 L swept
|-
| Cold exchanger C || colspan="2" | 0.132 L fixed gas volume
|-
| Hot exchanger H || colspan="2" | 0.132 L fixed gas volume
|}

The swept-volume ratio is S/L = 0.90 and both cylinder clearances are 1% of
swept volume. The two mechanisms are geometrically identical mirror assemblies
driven by the same physical crank pin. Opposite assembly branches and opposite
normal output coordinates produce the reflection. Both piston strokes are
0.2033 m; the swept-volume difference comes from piston bore.

{| class="wikitable"
! Mechanical dimension !! Small assembly !! Large assembly
|-
| Ground pivot distance || 0.2247 m || 0.2247 m
|-
| Shared crank radius || colspan="2" | 0.08987 m
|-
| Coupler length || 0.2247 m || 0.2247 m
|-
| Rocker length || 0.2629 m || 0.2629 m
|-
| Output coordinates in rocker frame || (0.1470, -0.2179) m || (0.1470, +0.2179) m
|-
| Four-bar assembly branch || +1 || -1
|-
| Piston connecting-rod length || 1.0166 m || 1.0166 m
|-
| Piston stroke || 0.2033 m || 0.2033 m
|-
| Implied piston bore || 0.1929 m || 0.2033 m
|}

The common crank has an angular offset of 304.375° relative to the solver's
thermodynamic angle origin. This is one common angular orientation, not an
independent phase shift between the two mechanisms. Horizontal slider axes are
centered on each output point's transverse excursion by the declared
construction rule.

'''Optimization scope:''' this work found a strong candidate within the
restricted family of identical reflected mechanisms. It did not prove that
mechanical symmetry is globally optimal. Coupler length, rocker length, fixed
pivot, output point, piston rod and slider layout were not varied independently
for S and L. Both mechanisms may be independently parameterized in a future
search while retaining the single shared crank pin.

This candidate was obtained from a one-bar, five-times-larger ideal-gas cycle
by multiplying every volume and CdA by 0.2 and dividing filling pressure by
0.2. This pressure-volume similarity is exact only in the first-level model.

== Heat transfer and hydraulic closure ==

{| class="wikitable"
! Parameter !! Value
|-
| Cold UA || 35.0 W/K
|-
| Hot UA || 35.0 W/K
|-
| L–H effective CdA || 3.122 × 10<sup>-5</sup> m²
|-
| S–C effective CdA || 5.576 × 10<sup>-5</sup> m²
|-
| H→S valve effective CdA || 3.122 × 10<sup>-5</sup> m²
|-
| C→L valve effective CdA || 1.115 × 10<sup>-4</sup> m²
|}

The hydraulic closure is a compressible choked/unchoked orifice model. CdA is
not a real open area and does not by itself establish velocity, Mach number,
exchanger pressure loss or manufacturability.

