{| class="wikitable"
! Quantity !! Result
|-
| Periodic solver || Converged after 7 successive cycles
|-
| Cooling energy per cycle || 607.20 J
|-
| Rejected heat per cycle || 892.66 J
|-
| Mechanical input per cycle || 285.46 J
|-
| Cooling power || 20.24 W
|-
| Heat-rejection power || 29.76 W
|-
| Thermodynamic mechanical input || 9.52 W
|-
| Cooling COP || 2.127
|-
| Fraction of reservoir-level Carnot COP || Approximately 51.0%
|-
| Pressure range over all volumes || 3.517 to 9.782 bar absolute
|-
| Temperature range over all volumes || 217.91 to 361.23 K
|-
| Maximum sampled mass flow || Approximately 7.56 × 10<sup>-4</sup> kg/s
|}

Mass and global energy residuals are approximately machine precision. The
maximum pressure-equalization error is 0.000336. Cold and hot isothermality
indicators are 0.01498 and 0.01602 respectively.

For illustration only, 85% transmission efficiency and 2 W continuous
auxiliary consumption would give:

<syntaxhighlight lang="text">
electrical input = 9.515 / 0.85 + 2 = 13.19 W
annual electricity = 13.19 * 8760 / 1000 = 115.6 kWh/year
</syntaxhighlight>

This is an order-of-magnitude scenario, not an appliance prediction. Cycling,
standby, fans, controls, defrost, cabinet heat leak and real motor efficiency
must be supplied explicitly.

== Mandatory limitations ==

* The physical-validity verdict is '''indeterminate''' because Mach number is
  unavailable without real flow areas.
* The passive-valve chronology is '''non-nominal''' and includes repeated
  transitions; the solver does not suppress these modeled behaviors.
* Helium is still modeled as an ideal gas with constant properties. Real-gas and
  property-variation checks are required from 217.9 to 361.2 K and up to 9.8 bar.
* Two 0.132 L gas volumes achieving 35 W/K have not yet been demonstrated by a
  realizable exchanger geometry.
* Seal leakage, actuator losses, mechanical friction, vibration, pressure-vessel
  design and cost are outside this result.
* Compressor-catalog COP and appliance-label energy use different system
  boundaries; direct superiority over commercial phase-change refrigeration is
  not claimed.

== Reproduction ==

The configuration is
<code>examples/domestic_freezer_helium_candidate_001.toml</code>. The result was
generated with version 0.1.0 of the Python DADA engine solver in SI units.

<syntaxhighlight lang="console">
python -m dada_solver.cli examples/domestic_freezer_helium_candidate_001.toml \
  --plot outputs/publication_helium_freezer_cycle.png

python -m dada_solver.mechanism_animation \
  examples/domestic_freezer_helium_candidate_001.toml \
  outputs/publication_helium_freezer_mechanism.gif --frames 90 --fps 18
</syntaxhighlight>

